 * derived: the #define keyword is not on the page
 */
#define COMPLETED 4

/* INTERACTIVE
 * row: INTERACTIVE (3) Some data has been read and parsed, and the object model is now available on the partially retrieved data set. Although the object model is available during this state, it is read-only.
 * source: corpus/learn/windows-ce-5.0/ms892645(v=msdn.10).html  borrowed from learn
 * derived: the #define keyword is not on the page
 */
#define INTERACTIVE 3

/* LOADED
 * row: LOADED (2) Reading of the persisted properties completed — reading and parsing data, but the object model is not yet available.
 * source: corpus/learn/windows-ce-5.0/ms892645(v=msdn.10).html  borrowed from learn
 * derived: the #define keyword is not on the page
 */
#define LOADED 2

/* LOADING
 * row: LOADING (1) The load is in progress — reading persisted properties, but not yet parsing data. For readyState definitions, data should be considered equivalent to binary large object (BLOB) properties.
 * source: corpus/learn/windows-ce-5.0/ms892645(v=msdn.10).html  borrowed from learn
 * derived: the #define keyword is not on the page
 */
#define LOADING 1

/* NODE_ATTRIBUTE
 * row: NODE_ATTRIBUTE (2) The node represents an attribute of an element. An attribute node can have the following child node types: Text and EntityReference. An attribute does not appear as the child node of any other node type; note that it is not considered a child node of an element.
 * source: corpus/learn/windows-ce-5.0/ms892577(v=msdn.10).html  borrowed from learn
 * derived: the #define keyword is not on the page
